(   2. Standard Construction Rules:) Tj
T*
(   - Rule 1 \(The Dividing Line\):) Tj
T*
(   * The line separating the unsectioned half from the sectioned half MUST BE DRAWN AS A) Tj
T*
(   CENTERLINE \(Chain Thin Line, Type G\)!) Tj
T*
(   * Under no circumstances should a solid continuous line be drawn at this boundary; a solid line) Tj
T*
(   represents a physical edge, whereas this division is purely an imaginary boundary between two) Tj
T*
(   viewing representations.) Tj
T*
(   - Rule 2 \(Omission of Hidden Lines\):) Tj
T*
(   * Hidden dashed lines are STRICTLY OMITTED from both the sectioned half \(where features are) Tj
T*
(   already visible outlines\) and the unsectioned half \(because the features are clearly defined in) Tj
T*
(   the adjacent sectioned half\).) Tj
T*
(   * Exception: A hidden line may be retained in the unsectioned half ONLY if needed to dimension) Tj
T*
(   an external feature that has no sectioned counterpart.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Dimensioning Protocol in Half Sections:) Tj
T*
(   - For internal cylindrical features \(bores, counterbores, keyways\):) Tj
T*
(   * Dimension lines are drawn originating from the sectioned feature, crossing slightly past the) Tj
T*
(   centerline, terminated with a SINGLE ARROWHEAD touching the sectioned wall!) Tj
T*
(   * The dimension value is prefixed with the diameter symbol 'phi' \(e.g. 'phi 50'\) to signify) Tj
T*
(   that the full diameter is represented, even though only half the bore is sectioned.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
