(   [Problem Statement]: Detail the HATCH command in AutoCAD, explaining the internal flood-fill boundary detection algorithm, the Select Objects mode, and island detection styles \(Normal, Outer, Ignore\).) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. HATCH Command Architecture:) Tj
T*
(   - Command: HATCH \(or 'H' [Enter]\)) Tj
T*
(   - Operates by calculating closed 2D mathematical loops and filling the bounded planar area with) Tj
T*
(   repeating vector patterns or solid color fills.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Boundary Definition Methods:) Tj
T*
(   - Pick Points \(Internal Point Detection\):) Tj
T*
(   * The user clicks a point inside an apparently closed area.) Tj
T*
(   * AutoCAD executes a Ray-Casting / Flood-Fill algorithm, projecting analysis rays outward in) Tj
T*
(   all directions to identify surrounding entities \(lines, arcs, polylines, splines\) forming a) Tj
T*
(   closed loop.) Tj
T*
(   * Fast and intuitive, but computationally expensive on huge drawings with millions of) Tj
T*
(   background entities.) Tj
T*
(   - Select Boundary Objects:) Tj
T*
(   * The user explicitly selects specific closed entities \(e.g., closed Polyline, Circle, Ellipse,) Tj
T*
(   or Region\).) Tj
T*
(   * 100% reliable, immune to boundary leaks and background clutter.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Island Detection Styles:) Tj
T*
(   - When nested closed boundaries \(islands\) exist inside an outer boundary \(e.g. a circular hole) Tj
T*
