(   [Problem Statement]: Detail the standard Hatch Patterns in AutoCAD \(ANSI, ISO, Solid, Gradient\), explaining their naming conventions, predefined scales, and typical material associations.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Standard Hatch Pattern Libraries in AutoCAD:) Tj
T*
(   AutoCAD stores pattern definitions in text files 'acad.pat' \(imperial\) and 'acadiso.pat') Tj
T*
(   \(metric ISO\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. ANSI Hatch Patterns \(American National Standards Institute\):) Tj
T*
(   - ANSI31: Single continuous parallel lines inclined at 45 degrees. Standard international) Tj
T*
(   representation for Cast Iron and general unclassified metals.) Tj
T*
(   - ANSI32: Pairs of continuous parallel lines inclined at 45 degrees. Represents Mild Steel and) Tj
T*
(   alloy steels.) Tj
T*
(   - ANSI33: Alternating continuous and dashed parallel lines at 45 degrees. Represents Bronze,) Tj
T*
(   Brass, Copper, and non-ferrous alloys.) Tj
T*
(   - ANSI34: Cross-hatched diagonal grid lines \(squares at 45?\). Represents Ceramic, porcelain,) Tj
T*
(   and refractory materials.) Tj
T*
(   - ANSI35: Diagonal continuous lines with transverse dashes. Represents Magnesium, aluminum, and) Tj
T*
(   light alloys.) Tj
T*
(   - ANSI36: Interrupted dashed parallel lines. Represents Zinc, lead, and babbitt bearing) Tj
T*
(   linings.) Tj
T*
(   - ANSI37: Cross-hatched grid forming diamonds. Represents Electrical insulation, rubber, and) Tj
T*
(   plastics.) Tj
T*
(   - ANSI38: Wavy interlocking lines. Represents Marble, slate, and glass.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. ISO & Other Standard Patterns:) Tj
T*
(   - SOLID: Fills the entire boundary with solid, opaque color \(used for structural plates < 2 mm,) Tj
T*
(   gaskets, and electrical schematics\).) Tj
T*
(   - GRADIENT: Smooth color transitions \(linear, cylindrical, spherical\) used for architectural) Tj
T*
(   presentations and conceptual industrial design.) Tj
T*
(   - USER DEFINED: Allows the user to specify custom angle, spacing, and double-hatching) Tj
T*
(   interactively at the command prompt.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
