(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the REGION command in AutoCAD and its application in 2D mechanical section analysis, detailing Boolean operations \(UNION, SUBTRACT, INTERSECT\) and MASSPROP.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Concept of 2D Regions in AutoCAD:) Tj
T*
(   - A Region is a two-dimensional enclosed planar surface object created from closed coplanar) Tj
T*
(   boundary curves \(lines, polylines, arcs, circles\).) Tj
T*
(   - Unlike wireframe polylines, a Region possesses physical 2D area properties, planar) Tj
T*
(   boundaries, and internal void loops.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Creating Regions \(REGION - REG\):) Tj
T*
(   - Command: REGION [Enter] -> Select objects forming closed loops -> [Enter].) Tj
T*
(   - AutoCAD analyzes topological connectivity and converts loops into Region objects.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Boolean Operations on Regions:) Tj
T*
(   - UNION \(UNI\): Merges two or more overlapping or contiguous regions into a single composite) Tj
T*
(   region.) Tj
T*
(   - SUBTRACT \(SU\): Subtracts one or more secondary regions \(e.g. cylindrical hole bores, slots\)) Tj
T*
(   from a primary target region, leaving exact internal voids.) Tj
T*
(   - INTERSECT \(IN\): Calculates and retains ONLY the common overlapping geometric area shared) Tj
T*
(   between two or more intersecting regions.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Engineering Mass Property Analysis \(MASSPROP\):) Tj
T*
(   - Command: MASSPROP [Enter] -> Select the completed 2D sectional Region.) Tj
T*
(   - AutoCAD immediately outputs an exhaustive mechanical properties report:) Tj
T*
(   * Surface Area \(sq. mm\)) Tj
T*
(   * Perimeter Length \(mm\)) Tj
T*
(   * Centroid Coordinates \(Center of Gravity: X, Y\)) Tj
T*
(   * Moments of Inertia \(Ixx, Iyy - critical for beam bending stress calculations!\)) Tj
T*
(   * Products of Inertia \(Ixy\)) Tj
T*
(   * Radii of Gyration \(Kx, Ky\)) Tj
T*
(   * Principal Moments and Directions about Centroid.) Tj
T*
ET

