(   [Problem Statement]: A cast steel bracket has a horizontal base plate 140 mm x 80 mm x 20 mm thick, a vertical back plate 80 mm wide x 20 mm thick x 70 mm high, and a central triangular reinforcing web 12 mm thick connecting them. A 30 mm hole is bored through the base, and a 25 mm hole through the back plate. Detail its Full Sectional Elevation along the longitudinal symmetry plane.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Bracket Component Geometry:) Tj
T*
(   - Base Plate: Length = 140 mm, Width = 80 mm, Thickness = 20 mm \(Z from 0 to 20\).) Tj
T*
(   - Back Plate: Located at left end \(X = 0 to 20\), Width = 80 mm \(Y from -40 to +40\), Height = 90) Tj
T*
(   mm total \(Z from 0 to 90\).) Tj
T*
(   - Central Triangular Web: Thickness = 12 mm \(centered along Y = 0, from Y = -6 to +6\). Connects) Tj
T*
(   top of base plate \(at X = 100, Z = 20\) to inner face of back plate \(at X = 20, Z = 80\).) Tj
T*
(   - Base Hole: Diameter = 30 mm, drilled vertically through base plate at X = 70 mm, Y = 0.) Tj
T*
(   - Back Plate Hole: Diameter = 25 mm, bored horizontally through back plate at X = 10 mm, Z = 55) Tj
T*
(   mm, Y = 0.) Tj
T*
(   - Cutting Plane: Passes vertically along the longitudinal symmetry plane \(Y = 0\) from end to) Tj
T*
(   end.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Full Sectional Elevation \(Looking along Y-direction at cut face\):) Tj
T*
(   - Back Plate Section:) Tj
T*
(   * Cut face extends from X = 0 to 20, Z = 0 to 90 mm.) Tj
T*
(   * The 25 mm horizontal hole cuts through from X = 0 to 20 at Z = 55 mm. Appears as an open) Tj
T*
(   unhatched rectangular gap 25 mm high, with a chain thin centerline along Z = 55.) Tj
T*
(   * Solid cut areas above and below the hole are hatched with ANSI31 at 45?.) Tj
T*
(   - Base Plate Section:) Tj
T*
(   * Cut face extends from X = 20 to 140, Z = 0 to 20 mm.) Tj
T*
(   * The 30 mm vertical hole cuts through from Z = 0 to 20 at X = 70 mm. Appears as an open) Tj
T*
(   unhatched gap 30 mm wide, with a chain thin centerline along X = 70.) Tj
T*
(   * Solid cut areas left and right of the hole are hatched with ANSI31 at 45?.) Tj
T*
(   - Triangular Reinforcing Web:) Tj
T*
(   * The cutting plane cuts directly along the longitudinal flat face of the 12 mm triangular web.) Tj
T*
(   * RULE OF NON-SECTIONING APPLIES: The triangular web is LEFT COMPLETELY UNHATCHED) Tj
T*
(   \(UNSECTIONED\)!) Tj
T*
(   * The boundary of the web is drawn with continuous thick visible outlines \(Type A\) running from) Tj
T*
(   \(20, 80\) to \(100, 20\).) Tj
T*
(   * Hatching the web would create the false impression of a solid block of metal.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
