(   [Problem Statement]: Discuss the rules for dimensioning sectional views in engineering drawings, detailing how to avoid placing dimension lines across hatched areas and how to handle leader callouts.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Placement of Dimensions on Sectional Views:) Tj
T*
(   - Preferred Placement: Dimensions should be placed OUTSIDE the hatched section view wherever) Tj
T*
(   practical, using extension lines that project away from the cut face.) Tj
T*
(   - Dimensioning to Centerlines: Centerlines extending out from holes and cylinders should be) Tj
T*
(   utilized as extension line anchors.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Dimensions Placed Inside Hatched Areas:) Tj
T*
(   - When placing a dimension numeral inside a hatched zone is unavoidable \(e.g. keyway depth,) Tj
T*
(   internal bore diameter\):) Tj
T*
(   * The hatching lines MUST BE INTERRUPTED \(broken\) around the dimension figure!) Tj
T*
(   * A clean white rectangular clearance area must surround the numeral so that hatch lines do not) Tj
T*
(   strike through or obscure the text.) Tj
T*
(   * Modern CAD systems \(AutoCAD\) accomplish this automatically via 'Text Island Detection' and) Tj
T*
(   associative dimension background masks.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Leader Line Callouts for Hole Features:) Tj
T*
(   - Complex internal features \(counterbores, countersinks, tapped threads\) are dimensioned using) Tj
T*
(   LEADER LINES terminating in an arrowhead touching the inner hole wall.) Tj
T*
(   - Standard ISO Callout Formats:) Tj
T*
(   * Counterbore: 'phi 20 V_THRU, [Counterbore symbol] phi 32 [Depth symbol] 10') Tj
T*
(   * Countersink: 'phi 15 V_THRU, [Countersink symbol] phi 28 x 90?') Tj
T*
(   * Tapped Thread: 'M24 x 2 - 6H [Depth symbol] 30') Tj
T*
(   - Leader lines should be inclined at 30?, 45?, or 60? to the horizontal, with a 2-3 mm) Tj
T*
(   horizontal landing at the text note.) Tj
T*
ET

