/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Describe the Broken-Out \(Partial\) Sectional View, detailing its application for inspecting localized interior features, the convention for break lines, and step-by-step CAD execution.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Concept and Purpose of Broken-Out Sections:) Tj
T*
(   - A Broken-Out Section \(also called a Partial Section or Local Section\) is employed when only a) Tj
T*
(   small, localized interior detail needs examination \(such as a keyway on a solid shaft, a) Tj
T*
(   set-screw hole in a hub, or an internal oil passage\) and a full or half section would) Tj
T*
(   unnecessarily remove valuable external features.) Tj
T*
(   - An imaginary break line is drawn around the feature, mentally 'breaking out' and peeling away) Tj
T*
(   the outer metal skin like an inspection window.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Break Line Standards \(Type C Line\):) Tj
T*
(   - The boundary of a broken-out section is drawn as a CONTINUOUS THIN FREEHAND LINE \(Type C,) Tj
T*
(   ~0.25 mm, Grade 2H\).) Tj
T*
(   - The line must be drawn with a gentle, irregular waviness.) Tj
T*
(   - Crucial Rule: The break line must NEVER coincide with a visible outline, a hidden edge, or a) Tj
T*
(   centerline of the object!) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Step-by-Step AutoCAD Execution Procedure:) Tj
T*
(   - Step 1: Draw the complete external view of the component on layer 'VISIBLE'.) Tj
T*
(   - Step 2: Draw the internal cavity feature \(e.g. keyway slot\) on layer 'VISIBLE' inside the) Tj
T*
(   component.) Tj
T*
ET

