(>> Solution to Question 26:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: A cast iron valve handwheel of 200 mm diameter has four elliptical spokes connecting a 40 mm diameter hub to a 20 mm circular rim. Explain how the spokes and rim are represented in a Full Sectional Elevation.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Handwheel Geometry:) Tj
T*
(   - Outer Rim: Toroidal ring with circular cross-section of diameter d = 20 mm; outer handwheel) Tj
T*
(   diameter = 200 mm.) Tj
T*
(   - Central Hub: Diameter D = 40 mm, Axial length = 35 mm, Keyed central bore = 18 mm.) Tj
T*
(   - Four Spokes: Elliptical cross-section \(major axis 16 mm, minor axis 10 mm\) connecting hub to) Tj
T*
(   rim at 90? intervals.) Tj
T*
(   - Cutting Plane: Passes along the central axis of the hub and through two diametrically) Tj
T*
(   opposite spokes.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Sectional Elevation Drafting Breakdown:) Tj
T*
(   - Rim Representation:) Tj
T*
(   * The cutting plane cuts directly through the top and bottom of the outer rim.) Tj
T*
(   * Cut surfaces appear as two TRUE CIRCLES of diameter 20 mm \(at top Z = +90 to +110, and bottom) Tj
T*
(   Z = -90 to -110 mm\).) Tj
T*
(   * Both cut circular rim sections ARE FULLY HATCHED with ANSI31 at 45?.) Tj
T*
(   - Hub Representation:) Tj
T*
(   * The hub is cut along its central bore.) Tj
T*
(   * Cut surfaces appear as rectangular walls above and below the 18 mm bore.) Tj
T*
(   * Both cut hub sections ARE FULLY HATCHED with ANSI31 at 45?.) Tj
T*
(   - Spoke Representation \(NON-SECTIONING CONVENTION\):) Tj
T*
(   * The two diametrically opposite spokes lie directly in the cutting plane.) Tj
T*
(   * MANDATORY CONVENTION: The spokes are SHOWN UNSECTIONED \(UNHATCHED\) in external elevation!) Tj
T*
(   * If the spokes were hatched, the handwheel would falsely appear as a solid plate or webbed) Tj
T*
(   disk.) Tj
T*
(   * To reveal the spoke cross-section, a REVOLVED SECTION \(an ellipse of 16 mm x 10 mm\) is drawn) Tj
T*
(   directly superimposed across one spoke using continuous thin lines \(Type B\)!) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
