12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the procedure to create an associative hatch with background color masking in AutoCAD, detailing the HATCHTOBACK command and draw order management.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Associative Hatching with Background Color:) Tj
T*
(   - Modern AutoCAD allows applying both a vector line pattern \(e.g. ANSI31\) and a background) Tj
T*
(   solid fill color \(e.g. pale yellow or gray\) simultaneously within a single hatch object.) Tj
T*
(   - In the Hatch Creation tab:) Tj
T*
(   * Pattern: Select ANSI31 \(Color set to 'ByLayer' or Cyan\).) Tj
T*
(   * Background Color: Select 'True Color' \(e.g. RGB 240, 240, 240\) from the palette.) Tj
T*
(   - Result: A professional presentation-grade graphic where internal cavities pop visually) Tj
T*
(   against white drawing sheets.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Draw Order Conflicts:) Tj
T*
(   - When a hatch is placed, it may inadvertently overlap and obscure existing geometry,) Tj
T*
(   dimensions, text notes, or centerlines.) Tj
T*
ET

