BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Detail the STRETCH command application in sectional views, explaining how to modify wall thicknesses and hole locations while preserving hatch associativity.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Hatch Associativity Preservation:) Tj
T*
(   - When a sectional view is created with Associative Hatching \(HPASSOC = 1\), AutoCAD maintains) Tj
T*
(   an internal bidirectional link between the hatch pattern and the bounding geometry vertices.) Tj
T*
(   - If the bounding geometry is modified, the hatch pattern automatically adapts, re-calculating) Tj
T*
(   its boundary and filling the new shape without requiring deletion and re-hatching.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Modifying Wall Thickness via STRETCH:) Tj
T*
(   - Scenario: A bracket wall thickness must be increased from 20 mm to 30 mm \(a 10 mm outward) Tj
T*
(   displacement\):) Tj
T*
(   * Command: STRETCH \(or 'S' [Enter]\).) Tj
T*
(   * Selection: Drag a Crossing Window \(green box, right-to-left\) enclosing the outer wall) Tj
T*
(   vertices AND crossing the attached dimension extension lines and hatch boundary.) Tj
T*
(   * Specify base point -> Snap to outer wall vertex.) Tj
T*
(   * Turn on Ortho \(F8\) -> Move cursor outward -> Type '10' [Enter].) Tj
T*
(   - Dynamic Result:) Tj
T*
(   * The outer wall shifts by 10 mm.) Tj
T*
(   * The attached dimension line updates automatically from 20.00 to 30.00 mm.) Tj
T*
(   * The underlying hatch pattern instantly expands by 10 mm to fill the enlarged wall space) Tj
T*
(   seamlessly!) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Precaution:) Tj
T*
(   - Never explode an associative hatch prior to stretching; exploded hatch lines will not stretch) Tj
T*
(   and will leave messy orphaned line fragments.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
