T*
(   2. Step-by-Step Assembly Drafting:) Tj
T*
(   - Step 1 \(Shaft Centerline Datum\): Establish primary horizontal and vertical centerlines on) Tj
T*
(   layer 'CENTER'.) Tj
T*
(   - Step 2 \(Draw Shaft First\): Draw the central drive shaft in external elevation \(unsectioned\)) Tj
T*
(   on layer 'VISIBLE'. Add keyways and shoulders.) Tj
T*
(   - Step 3 \(Insert Bearings & Seals\):) Tj
T*
(   * Insert standard rolling bearing blocks against shaft shoulders.) Tj
T*
(   * Insert elastomeric oil seals into their housing grooves.) Tj
T*
(   - Step 4 \(Draw Housings & End Caps\):) Tj
T*
(   * Draw the casting walls of the main gearbox housing and bolted end covers.) Tj
T*
(   - Step 5 \(Apply Contrasting Section Lining\):) Tj
T*
(   * Main Housing: Hatch with ANSI31 at 45?, scale 1.0.) Tj
T*
(   * Bolted End Cap: Hatch with ANSI31 at 135?, scale 1.0.) Tj
T*
(   * Bearing Rings: Hatch with ANSI32 \(steel\) at 45?, scale 0.5 \(finer pitch\).) Tj
T*
(   * Shaft & Fasteners: Left unhatched in elevation.) Tj
T*
(   - Step 6: Execute HATCHTOBACK to ensure all shaft outlines and dimensions remain crisp and) Tj
T*
(   prominent.) Tj
T*
() Tj
