/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Summarize the complete quality assurance audit checklist for validating sectional views prior to engineering manufacturing release.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Engineering Quality Audit Protocol for Sectional Views:) Tj
T*
(   1. Cutting Plane Line & Arrow Validation:) Tj
T*
(   - Verify that Cutting Plane Line \(Type H\) is present on the parent view with thick ends \(~0.5) Tj
T*
(   mm\) and thick corner bends.) Tj
T*
(   - Confirm viewing direction arrows point in the correct line of sight.) Tj
T*
(   - Check that reference identification letters \(e.g. A-A\) are clearly legible and match the) Tj
T*
(   title 'SECTION A-A'.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Section Lining \(Hatching\) Integrity:) Tj
T*
(   - Verify that hatching lines are continuous thin \(0.25 mm\) and inclined at 45? to principal) Tj
T*
(   axes.) Tj
T*
(   - Confirm that all solid cut surfaces are hatched, and open voids/holes are unhatched.) Tj
T*
(   - Check that adjacent mating components in assemblies have opposing hatch angles \(45? vs 135?\)) Tj
T*
(   or different spacing pitches.) Tj
T*
(   - Confirm that dimension numerals placed in hatched zones have clean clearance breaks.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Non-Sectioning Compliance Check:) Tj
T*
(   - Verify that solid shafts, bolts, nuts, washers, keys, cotters, rivets, and dowel pins cut) Tj
T*
(   longitudinally are UNHATCHED in elevation.) Tj
T*
(   - Verify that thin webs, ribs, and wheel spokes cut longitudinally are UNHATCHED.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. View Separation & Geometry:) Tj
T*
(   - In Half Sections: Verify that the dividing line is strictly a CHAIN THIN CENTERLINE \(never a) Tj
T*
(   solid line!\).) Tj
T*
(   - In Offset Sections: Verify that no lines are drawn at 90-degree step transitions.) Tj
T*
(   - Confirm that all section boundaries are watertight closed loops with associative hatching) Tj
T*
(   intact.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
ET

